       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nHere are some ways I could proceed:\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 10 mg now and add a second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic. Adding one is usually more effective than going above 10 mg.\n3. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written.** This is an intentional above-label dose. Please confirm that's what you want, and tell me if you'd like a note on the order with the rationale, such as \"dose exceeds usual max, confirmed by attending.\"\n\nWhich would you like?"
